{"answer": "Alright, imagine you have a super cool toy box filled with blocks. Normally, when you play with blocks, you can only use one block at a time to build something. This is like how regular computers work—they use tiny bits that can be either a 0 or a 1, like having one block at a time.

Now, imagine if you had magical blocks that could be both a 0 and a 1 at the same time! This is what quantum computers do. They use special bits called "qubits" that can be both 0 and 1 at the same time, like having a block that can be two things at once. This means they can solve certain problems much faster than regular computers because they can try many possibilities all at once.

So, quantum computing is like having a magical toy box that lets you build things in super cool and fast ways that regular toy boxes can't do!"}

